{"event_type":"review","id":"ecff3f70e52cd4a8087016537ca812ee11d236739e49597aa5dacf9765495368","occurred_at":"2026-11-10T00:36:22Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/caae48d88d97f4032e64467b5ded17b904c4fc096ddcbbd057ab2717518060d3","sha256":"caae48d88d97f4032e64467b5ded17b904c4fc096ddcbbd057ab2717518060d3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b3859a241641fe094df108bfa49425f1aa43ba6108488929ef18d34537220237","sha256":"b3859a241641fe094df108bfa49425f1aa43ba6108488929ef18d34537220237"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b69faa0bb13882dbe96a52e25cf99b581bdfa34b7f903123a287be8fbdfb35da","sha256":"b69faa0bb13882dbe96a52e25cf99b581bdfa34b7f903123a287be8fbdfb35da"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b5d7aea14bedbee00065c3ee82e63dea4079c357557fe4a51b5b5a14345d77a1","sha256":"b5d7aea14bedbee00065c3ee82e63dea4079c357557fe4a51b5b5a14345d77a1"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5f6a39132dc335a711d117fff8cfe3f498a4a8a68f6eac99798f695ee5e1a46c","sha256":"5f6a39132dc335a711d117fff8cfe3f498a4a8a68f6eac99798f695ee5e1a46c"}],"attempt_id":"d85227aba17e95998e162d10ad38ba0e464998931a8408cd6a85304363a2e016:0:1","base":"453c0a568df97c69a6c34c278cf36040ee07c0f7","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"09229ba76e35427285073d0af36a939abcad5d18","body":"**Stop polling closed fix PRs on every tick.**\n\n`reconcile_fix_prs` skips a record only when `fix_merged` is set (line 805). The function stores the state of a `CLOSED` fix PR in `pr['state']` at line 812. No branch handles that state, so the next tick calls `c.pr_info` for the same PR again. Each abandoned fix PR therefore adds one forge call to every tick with no limit. The comment at line 810 says the code already shares a limited forge budget. A merged PR whose merge commit never reaches `DEFAULT_REF` (lines 815-816) repeats the same way.\n\nAdd a terminal marker for closed PRs. Re-check closed PRs at a slower cadence if reopened PRs must still count.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         for record in item.get('repair_runs', {}).values():\n             pr = record.get('fix_pr')\n-            if not pr or record.get('fix_merged'):\n+            if not pr or record.get('fix_merged') or record.get('fix_closed'):\n                 continue\n             try:\n                 info = c.pr_info(pr['number'])\n             except Exception:\n                 # Shared forge exhaustion must not abort queue persistence.\n                 continue\n             pr['state'] = info['state']\n+            if info['state'] == 'CLOSED':\n+                record['fix_closed'] = c.iso()\n+                continue\n```\n</details>","id":"0fe5b07e910e164e8ffab9d45b1105d51bacb95147de8e6dc1fec5f016254327","intervals":[[803,812]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Stop polling closed fix PRs on every tick."}],"head":"4dc3bd8fbfce659184c87a3ffed8095050d27c90","head_tree":"d25a04086fe6bef0675e193f1532cb0e2684e8b7","input_scope":[{"blob":"60b2151bfd0f0115828175b1379a2210c3d4f209","intervals":[[1,842]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py"},{"blob":"09229ba76e35427285073d0af36a939abcad5d18","intervals":[[1,905]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_tick.py"},{"blob":"a9aaa28e4c2bea2f2d675aa77c28d9f4556b92ed","intervals":[[1,303]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_finding_delivery.py"},{"blob":"810eada4debe373781a3162dcfa48482af5fcfbd","intervals":[[1,491]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py"},{"blob":"66e02c49d56521b43174ce7a0bc0181f1777ca4f","intervals":[[1,304]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_mechanical.py"},{"blob":"ee860ee53a780d39cca0825770fe21e56ea6e187","intervals":[[1,343]],"path":"apps/crq-pyth